<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! sense.sensorium.retires ~ a sensorium retires on its grounds

`lares sense retire <name> grounds=<grounds> approve=true` runs on a person's hand at a real terminal and retires the named sensorium in its manifest on one of the named grounds; `un-retire` reverses it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ retire

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`retire` params=`name/pioneer-1 grounds/superseded approve/true ~ retire a sensorium`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ name · grounds · approve

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`name` params=`takes/name needs/required seat/1 as/<name> ~ the sensorium named in the manifest`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`grounds` params=`takes/word needs/required ~ the grounds, one of the named set`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`approve` params=`~ name the intent`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ hand

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`hand` params=`who/hand ~ runs direct over manifest.json; a person at a real terminal, and the verb names its intent with --approve where it asks one`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ verb-error · hand-act-only

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`verb-error` params=`~ no name, no --approve, unknown grounds, or the retire refused; the hint lists the grounds`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`hand-act-only` params=`~ a seat reached a hand verb; name the command for the operator`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ retired

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`retired` params=`exit/0 ~ the manifest after`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins`>>

!! skins ~ cli

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins/cli`>>

!!! lares sense retire

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`skin` name=`cli` params=`handler/host spells/[[lares sense retire]] ~ the terminal`>>
```

